      "markiere": { "verb": [1], "schluessel": [3] },
      "regel": "First look: the *pretérito indefinido* talks about finished times: *ayer, anoche, el sábado, el lunes*. The full rule is an A2 topic; here you only meet the *yo* forms of a few common verbs. Regular: -ar verbs end in *-é* (comprar → _compré_), -er / -ir verbs in *-í* (comer → _comí_). Very common irregular verbs: ir → _fui_, hacer → _hice_, tener → _tuve_, venir → _vine_. Question to one person: *¿Qué hiciste el sábado?* A bracketed word like (yo) says who is speaking; you don't write it.",
      "tabelle": {
        "kopf": ["Infinitive", "Indefinido (yo)"],
        "zeilen": [["cocinar", "cociné"], ["comprar", "compré"], ["comer", "comí"], ["ir", "fui"], ["hacer", "hice"], ["tener", "tuve"]]
      }
